@Ryan Casey I know it took a while for us to start the review, but this 1B seems to be missing in the current version. If this is expected, let's remove it.

Also the 3# items - the first of them would be "Tab"able (purple) and the rest would be arrow navigation (teal), as you marked them up.

Maybe they could be 1B, 1C, ...., 1F and then the current "1C" would become the 1G (to make sure "See what to do..." is focusable after the list and before the "Mark as fixed)?

@Ryan Casey @Wolasi Konu Ran this by Meridel and she's good with this copy!

One small edit that we didn't discuss today: tweaking the structure of the 1st sentence. All else is good to go! 

I can put these into the spec whenever that's ready. Thanks!

@Ryan Casey we could remove this note altogether or have it as "paragraph" since it is not a part of a complex widget. 

We could use this item as "aria-describedby" for the item A (section)

Editing to add: and this "aria-describedby" would work similarly how, I assume, the alert's description was expected to work - it would be announced after the item B (heading) and role of section, once a screen reader enters this section

@Laura Lopez @Wolasi Konu @Tony Cinotto - just being anticipatory:
I wonder if this is the section that Legal may be wanting to ensure is accessible from about:logins? 
If so, is it worth considering having a section on either Monitor pages (logged in/out) about Firefox like this—which could negate the need for two links?

